This image contains strongSwan 6.1.0, built from the unmodified upstream release.
See strongSwan-COPYING for the upstream licence and exceptions. The complete
corresponding upstream source archive, release signature/key, verifier, build
script, Dockerfile and provenance are bundled in ../source. No written source
offer is substituted for these actual files.

Runtime dependencies are installed through Alpine's authenticated APK
repositories. Exact build and runtime APK versions are recorded in ../source.
OpenSSL and musl are distribution components, not part of the strongSwan archive.
Alpine package sources are at https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports
and https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/ . Distribution release review
must include dependency licences and the matching source artifacts; this notice
is not a claim that a dependency source/notice review has been completed.

The node uses its own bounded VICI codec. No govici code is redistributed.
Shipping the daemon does not start it, create SAs or authorize IPsec traffic.
